WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.735
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy- and Grammy-winning,

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.171
Oscar-nominated actress,
musician, and producer

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.872
you know from movies
such as "Chicago,"

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:08.508
"Bringing Down the House,"
and "Girls Trip."

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:11.311
She stars in "The Equalizer,"
which airs Sunday nights on CBS.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.545
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.913
-Now!

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.048
-I heard you the first time.

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:18.384
You saying it louder

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.820
is not gonna make me
any more afraid of you.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.622
-Watch this.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.257
[ Both grunting ]

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:26.959
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:31.631
♪♪

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.232
-Please welcome
back to the show

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:35.534
our friend Queen Latifah!

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.670
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.906
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:47.547
♪♪

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:55.187
♪♪

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:58.624
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.693
[ Laughs ]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.494
-Hello!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.494 --> 00:01:05.731
-Whoo!
-Hello!

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.735
-Oh, my gosh, I was just coming
from this board meeting

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.236
at Twitter.
-Oh, no!

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.537
-I was just like,
I just want to talk to y'all.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.839
-You're on the board.
You're on the board, yeah.

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:16.543
-i just wanted to talk to them
about maybe just talking

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.012
about selling me the company.
-Well!

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.980
-They just kind of
laughed a little.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.248
-That is the future, though.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.649
-Said they just had
a guy in there.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:25.651
-Oh, so, you had
the same approach as Fred.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.553
You just wanted to talk to them?
-I figured

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.456
they had all the money.
You know?

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.792
So...
-You guys think alike.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.728
-They said they already had
a guy they were considering.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.497
-I'm sorry, that must have been
hard to hear.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.599
I'm very, very sorry.
But good news.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.800
I have some good news, though.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.936
Congratulations
on "The Equalizer."

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:46.572
This was the most-watched
network season premiere.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.974
[ Cheers and applause ]
7 million people.

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:52.412
Not only -- This, to me,
must be so exciting.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:55.915
Not only does America love it
but your family specifically

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.117
is a big fan.
-Yes, more importantly

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:01.521
than the entire world
is my grandmother...

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.923
-Okay.
-...who is, like, right there

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.425
in a recliner, watching it.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.993
And she's just,
"I just love that show."

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.162
-How old
is your grandmother now?

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.564
-My grandmother is 94.
-94.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.600
[ Cheers and applause ]
-94.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.703
And she's like,
"I just love that action."

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.239
-She's okay with
all those bad guys

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.640
pulling guns
on her granddaughter?

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.975
-She's okay
with her granddaughter

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.244
whupping on them bad guys.
-Yeah!

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.046
You do a lot of whupping
in this show.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:30.783
-I do.
-Now, your father was an ex-cop.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.419
-Mm-hmm.
-And how does he --

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.021
Was this something where --
Do you find inspiration from him

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:37.890
when you play these
sort of badass characters?

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.193
-I do, I do, 'cause he was,
you know, "Get 'em, Dana!"

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:42.962
He been saying that
since I was little.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.064
"Stick 'em, Dana, stick 'em."
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.466
-"Daddy, who?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.769
No, my father taught me
so much stuff

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.471
before I was even, like,
you know, 7.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.041
And I'm like, "Dad, you know,

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.743
I can't use any of this
in school."

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.078
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.614
You know, he's like, "You can
do this thing here,

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.915
and then you can break
their wrist --

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.184
you know, break the thumb.
You can pull like this,

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.752
and then you
pull the whole socket out."

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.254
And I'm like, "Daddy,

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.790
I can't use any of these moves
in school,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.092
'cause I would be expelled.
-Thumb breaking,

00:03:14.092 --> 00:03:16.161
you definitely got to wait
till at least high school.

00:03:16.161 --> 00:03:19.398
-Like, "Come on," you know?
This is, like, major stuff."

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:22.735
But, no, no, no, he's --
he's a big inspiration.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.171
You know, he was
S.W.A.T. and tactical,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.006
and a lot of
my family members are.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.242
And so they
get excited about it.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.645
But it's cute because
a lot of the guys

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:35.181
actually love
the family aspect of it.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:37.383
-Of the show. That's wonderful.
That's a nice element.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.252
-They like the relationship
with the daughter and the son.

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:42.555
And then, like,
but all the women are like,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.991
"You kicking butt!
And I love it!

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.626
And you are bad!"
You know?

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.894
And I love it.
And they just get mad at me.

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:52.599
My Aunt Angel, she gets mad
if football runs over.

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:55.801
-Oh, that they have to delay
the start of her "Equalizer"?

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.070
-She's always sending me
some sort of text.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.939
She's like, "Don't make me --"

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.774
Now, this is
a very church-going woman.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.610
You know, like,
director of the choir,

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.178
the whole nine.
She's like,

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.647
"Don't make me come up there
and have to talk to Oprah.

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:11.117
And who is Adele anyway?"

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.285
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.354
"L-O-L."
-She knows what she wants.

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:17.423
-And then, the next week,
she's like,

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.324
"You don't make me
have to come up there.

00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:21.894
And what is a football anyway?"

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:25.498
So, every week, it's, like,
she just has me laughing.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.399
-I want to know where it is
she wants to come up to.

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.702
-To New York.
-To New York. I see.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.604
-They're all, like,
in Maryland and Virginia.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.239
So, like, "Don't make me come."
-Whoo!

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.107
-Maryland and Virginia, hey.
-There you go.

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:38.110
-So, they're like, you know --
They watch it together

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.745
sometimes,
which is really nice.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:43.583
-I will say, growing up,
as a kid who was around

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.350
during the sort of
'90s rap boom,

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.786
it is always fascinating to me
that people like you,

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:51.257
people like Ice-T,
people like LL Cool J

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.725
are all leads of sort of
network television shows,

00:04:53.725 --> 00:04:55.762
playing police officers,
no less.

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.663
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:59.131
Is this something
that surprises you,

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:00.333
or does it make sense?

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:05.604
-We understand
both sides of the coin.

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.407
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:11.110
We can speak from a place
of [Chuckles]

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.112
It does not surprise me
at all.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.648
I mean, we were -- you know,

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:17.650
this was, like,
a burgeoning music form.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.653
And so we were all, like,
hustlers out there going for it.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:24.123
And -- And I --
And we all toured together.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:27.226
So we would -- There would be
like 10 acts, at least,

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:31.163
on these tours.
And so we were all friends.

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:33.632
And so, when Will
got "Fresh Prince,"

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:34.967
it was like, "Oh.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.002
Oh, if Will can do a show,
we can do a show."

00:05:37.002 --> 00:05:39.405
And then, with the movies,
and then there was Cube,

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.807
and, of course, L is, like,
"Well, if Loc can do a show,

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.309
I'm getting a show."

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:46.212
And then Ice-T is
the boss of all of us,

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:48.447
so he's like, "I pretty much
will do whatever I want to do,

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:50.349
when I want to do it."

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:54.120
But then --
Who else is out there?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.855
So everybody kind of
looked at each other.

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:59.024
Oh, Cube -- So, Cube starts
doing movies, and great ones.

00:05:59.024 --> 00:06:01.160
And so we're like, "Well,
if Cube can do movies,

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.029
then we can do movies, too."

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.464
So I think we all kind of, like,
inspired each other

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.500
to go for it.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.401
Like, to go bigger
than just the music.

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:11.604
-I mean, a lot of it --
Look, it's all performance,

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:13.339
and it's all --
you know, it requires

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:14.874
a skill and
an attention to detail

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.775
and a craft.
And I think you see

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:19.345
it makes sense when you see that
a whole generation of people

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.180
who were doing that in the '90s
are doing this other thing now.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.748
It does make sense
you would all be good at both.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.550
-Which is very, very cool.
I think it's cool.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.019
-Do you remember
your first lyrics

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.754
that you wrote for yourself?

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.356
-I can't remember these lyrics,

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:33.425
but somebody just sent me
my demo, and I was like 16.

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:35.194
[ Laughter ]
-Have you listened to it?

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:38.197
-Yeah. It sounds crazy.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:41.233
I'm glad that someone was --
Thank you, Dante Ross for...

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:45.304
Thank you, Fab Five Freddy,
for giving to it Dante Ross,

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.672
who gave it to Monica Lynch,

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:49.375
who gave it
to Tommy Boy Records,

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.911
who signed me
off of this one demo

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.679
that my boy
spent the rent money on.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.114
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.682
-When you listen to it,
does it --

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:59.017
Do you think, "Alright,
they made the right call"?

00:06:59.017 --> 00:07:01.820
Or do you feel like -- Does it
make you feel cringey,

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.289
listening to your early stuff?

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:06.391
-It feels like it was the '80s.
-Yeah.

00:07:06.391 --> 00:07:08.393
[ Laughter ]
-I mean, like, I could tell

00:07:08.393 --> 00:07:10.896
by the cadence and the things
that I was talking about.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.800
But I don't think they had heard
anything like that,

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.567
because it has, like,
a reggae hook.

00:07:15.567 --> 00:07:17.703
I'm singing on the record,
as well as rapping.

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:21.273
So I don't think anybody was
really doing that at the time.

00:07:21.273 --> 00:07:24.243
And I just sounded different
from everybody out there.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:27.246
So that's what
I think got me in the door.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:30.782
-I think there's a great deal,
obviously, that's about talent,

00:07:30.782 --> 00:07:34.086
but another big thing is
choosing a name, Queen Latifah.

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:36.855
Now I can't imagine
choosing anything else.

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:39.624
But you had to have had some
Plan B's, Plan C's in there.

00:07:39.624 --> 00:07:41.861
-Pbht.
Well...

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:43.763
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:45.865
There's a lot of jokes
in that, Seth.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.499
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:50.136
I'mma leave it alone.
Gonna leave it right on alone.

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:52.271
Um... [ Laughs ]

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:53.839
Uh, none of them worked.

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:55.608
I mean, like my original --

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:59.278
Like, my original rap name
was La Wordski.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:01.847
-La Wordski.
-You know, which was like

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:04.817
"the word" or "la word,"
and the "ski" part.

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:08.287
-It's interesting you say "ski,"
'cause LL Cool J was here,

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:11.657
and he said it was --
he had Coolski or something.

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:14.626
I think "ski" was originally
part of his name, as well.

00:08:14.626 --> 00:08:16.662
He said
that the issue with "ski,"

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:19.532
maybe in the '80s,
had a cocaine connotation.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:22.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:24.503
Oh, this is
the first you're hearing?

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:27.739
-What?!
[ Laughter ]

00:08:27.739 --> 00:08:32.278
It's almost like when
I went to the Twitter meeting.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:34.413
-Yeah, oh, my God!
Finding this out!

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:36.615
Two things on the same day.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:39.552
No, yeah, you didn't --
I mean, it was everybody --

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:41.119
everybody was something-ski.

00:08:41.119 --> 00:08:43.855
And you know, you just kinda...
-I think it's good.

00:08:43.855 --> 00:08:46.158
-We were trendy at the time,
but we had sense enough

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:49.595
to maybe not go with that
as our main names,

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.063
once we got signed.

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:53.098
-"Queen Latifah" certainly
has aged a lot nicer

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:55.467
than I think that would.
-Yes, I had no idea

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.136
that people were gonna
say that whole thing.

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.838
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:03.142
I was just -- My first record,
literally, it's a record --

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:05.211
vinyl -- that came out.

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:06.779
It just says "Latifah."

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:08.113
Because I had singles first.

00:09:08.113 --> 00:09:09.581
I didn't even have
an album deal.

00:09:09.581 --> 00:09:11.951
So, it came out,
and it said "Latifah."

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:13.853
And I worked
at the record store,

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:15.921
and I wanted to sell them
my own record.

00:09:15.921 --> 00:09:17.189
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:18.824
People would come in
and ask for that "Latifah."

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:20.226
"Can I get
that Latifah record?"

00:09:20.226 --> 00:09:22.360
I'm like, "Yeah.
You want me to sign it?"

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.031
You know what I mean?
-Did they believe it was you?

00:09:25.031 --> 00:09:27.266
I think, if you bought an album,
and the person

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:28.767
at the record store
said it was them,

00:09:28.767 --> 00:09:29.968
most people
wouldn't believe them.

00:09:29.968 --> 00:09:31.237
-They didn't believe me
at first,

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:32.705
but then the manager would
come up, "Yeah, it's her.

00:09:32.705 --> 00:09:34.806
It's really her.
Yeah, she's the..."

00:09:34.806 --> 00:09:38.177
And then, when it came time
to sign my long-form album deal,

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:41.446
I was like, "Yeah, Queen.
Queen, Queen.

00:09:41.446 --> 00:09:45.251
Queen Latifah."
You know? "Queen."

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:49.688
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Sometimes, you know --

00:09:49.688 --> 00:09:52.024
Sometimes you gotta
call your shot ahead of time.

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:53.559
Sometimes you got to let them
know who they are,

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:54.960
and then they'll find out
that you were right.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.863
-I know. That there would be
this Queen from New Jersey.

00:09:57.863 --> 00:09:59.664
-Well --
-My mother laughed at first.

00:09:59.664 --> 00:10:02.034
-When you told her you decided
to go with Queen Latifah?

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:04.303
-She was like, "Queen?"
[ Laughter ]

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:07.139
-[ Laughs ]

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:08.774
I guess, you know, hearing

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:11.376
your 17-year-old daughter
say that is kind of funny.

00:10:11.376 --> 00:10:13.112
-Then all these years later,
you're like,

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:14.780
"Now, 'The Equalizer,'
that I understand," yeah,

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.382
-Yes.
-From Queen to "Equalizer,"

00:10:17.382 --> 00:10:20.518
and every step of the way,
it's just been a joy to watch.

00:10:20.518 --> 00:10:21.820
Thanks for being here.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.355
I'm always so happy
to spend time with you.

00:10:23.355 --> 00:10:25.257
-Seth, I'm always so happy
to come back.

00:10:25.257 --> 00:10:28.226
I love this show.
-Queen Latifah, everybody.

00:10:28.226 --> 00:10:30.796
"The Equalizer,"
Sunday nights on CBS.

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:32.264
We'll be right back
with Sarah Sherman.

